id: pm-hx23u5
title: "GH-854: transactional extension mutation guards for enforceable domain invariants"
description: "Extensions can observe committed writes but cannot veto invalid core mutations. Add a public capability-gated pre-commit mutation guard receiving before, proposed after, changed fields, operation, and a host-bound read-only SDK; stable allow or deny errors must run inside the same item/history transaction across CLI, PmClient, workspace transactions, restore/delete, and bulk paths."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:extensions","area:sdk",gh-issue,invariants,mutation,security,transactions
created_at: "2026-08-01T13:27:20.518Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T15:05:15.482Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-01T14:39:31.642Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-01T14:39:31.642Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Public guard contracts expose before, proposed after, changed fields, operation, and host-bound read-only SDK context; Deny results and expected public errors abort item and history persistence atomically with stable codes and remediation; CLI, embedded client, workspace transaction, restore, delete, and bulk mutation routes share the guard; Capability contracts, testing helpers, docs, and isolated extension acceptance prove enforcement"
parent: pm-usfg
severity: high
repro_steps: "Register an immutable content-addressed custom type, reference one item, then mutate it through pm update; the extension can only detect the invalid write afterward"
expected_result: A capability-gated public guard can atomically allow or deny every core item mutation with stable remediation
actual_result: Available hooks are post-commit or warning-only and cannot enforce invariants
affected_version: 2026.8.1
component: sdk/extensions/mutations
